@defgroup micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated Deprecated
@brief Definitions kept for compatibility with earlier releases.

@details
The deprecated definitions are kept so that the tests written for the
earlier releases still compile; they will be removed in a future major
release. The compiler reports each use, with a message that names the
replacement and the version that deprecated it (most of them since
6.0.0).

@par Availability
The deprecated definitions exist only when the application defines the
macro `MICRO_OS_PLUS_MICRO_TEST_PLUS_DEPRECATED_ENABLED` (see
@ref micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-config). Without it, the tests that
still use them do not compile, which shows what remains to be migrated.

@par Migration
Build once with the macro defined and the deprecation warnings enabled,
and rewrite each reported use as its message suggests. While migrating,
the applications that build with `-Werror` can disable the warnings
temporarily with `-Wno-deprecated-declarations`.

@code{.cpp}
namespace mt = micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus;

// Deprecated.
using namespace mt::operators;
using namespace mt::literals;
t.expect (compute_answer () == 42_i) << "answer is 42";

// Replacement.
t.expect (mt::eq (compute_answer (), 42)) << "answer is 42";
@endcode

@par Deprecated groups
Three groups of deprecated definitions have topics of their own:
- the overloaded comparison and logical operators (see
  @ref micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated-operators),
  replaced by the function comparators and the logical functions;
- the user-defined literals and the type wrappers (see
  @ref micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated-literals),
  replaced by the plain values passed to the function comparators;
- the logical functions `_and()`, `_or()`, and `_not()` (see
  @ref micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated-logical-functions),
  replaced by `all_of()`, `any_of()`, and `negate()`.

@par Other deprecated definitions
- the v5.0.1 names of the classes: `static_runner` (replaced by `runner`),
  `subtest` (replaced by `test_case`), `detail::runner_totals` (replaced by
  `counters`), and `detail::timestamps` and `detail::timestamp`, which are
  internal and not replaced;
- `runner (const char*)`, replaced by `runner()` followed by
  `add_top_suite()` (since 4.1.0);
- `runner::initialise (argc, argv, top_suite_name)`, replaced by
  `initialise (argc, argv)` followed by `add_top_suite()`;
- `runner::exit_code()`, replaced by `runner::run_suites()`;
- `runner::suite()`, replaced by `runner::add_suite()`;
- `runner::suites_count()`, replaced by `added_suites_count()` or
  `total_suites_count()`;
- `runner::verbosity()`, and `runner::reporter()` with its `verbosity()`
  member, replaced by `runner::verbosity_level()`;
- `runner::timings()` and `test_case::timings()`, and the members of
  `detail::stopwatch` kept from the v5.0.1 timestamps, which are
  internal and not replaced;
- the `counters` members `successful_checks()`, `executed_subtests()`,
  and `was_successful()`, replaced by `passed_checks()`,
  `executed_test_cases()`, and `passed()` (the deprecated mutators
  `increment_successful_checks()` and `increment_executed_subtests()`
  were removed, since the counters are updated only by the framework);
- `test_case::assume()`, replaced by `test_case::require()`;
- the overloads of `test_case::expect()` and `test_case::require()` that
  accept an argument that is always true (a string literal or a function
  name), replaced by writing the condition;
- the `static_suite` constructor whose callable takes a `static_suite&`,
  replaced by a callable taking a `suite&`;
- `reflection::short_name()`, replaced by `utility::extract_file_name()`;
- the `type_traits` namespace, with the concepts and the value wrapper
  templates of v5.0.1, replaced by the `extension` namespace;
- the traits of the `type_traits` namespace: `function_traits` and
  `list`, which are not replaced, and `identity`, replaced by
  `std::type_identity`.
